      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is not that retributive justice is inherently flawed, but rather that its emphasis on abstract punishment can become detached from the victim's lived experience of harm. The criticism is that pure retribution can prioritize state vengeance over actual healing and accountability for the victim. True justice requires acknowledging the gravity of the offense while ensuring the process serves the goals of repair, satisfaction for the harmed party, and prevention of future harm.",
